  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 256 AM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nOutside of patchy fog, northern MI wx continues to be quiet.\nSome layered cloud is seen well upstream, over far northern MN\nand adjoining parts of Canada. This is associated with a digging\nshortwave, which will cross northern MI late today. Warm\nadvection will increase ahead of this feature, and before a cold\nfront moves in late today. Though available forcing is\nreasonable, moisture is not. \n\nPer sat imagery, early morning fog is currently concentrated\nin central/western Chippewa Co, and to a lesser degree ne lower\nMI. This will burn off this morning, but will locally inhibit\ndiurnal heating at least for a bit. Models have a smidge of \nMuCape this morning near the MN Arrowhead, but not any closer \nthan that. A band of sct showers is likely to pass north of \neastern upper MI late this afternoon/ early this evening. \nCertainly not impossible for us to squeeze out a sprinkle or \nshower in the eastern UP late today, Chippewa Co in particular. \nBut this chance remains too small to mention.\n\nCold front settles to the MI/OH border tonight, with trailing\nhigh pressure passing just north of Lk Superior. Post-frontal \npressure gradient will be tighter in the north than south, which\nmakes the return of fog tonight less likely in the north. \nPatchy/areas of fog are possible elsewhere, especially in nw/n \ncentral lower MI. We won't quite as warm behind the front\nThursday as today, but still quiet.\n\n500mb ridge axis will be building and sharpening into the Great\nLakes area Friday/Saturday. Quiet and somewhat warmer again. An\nincreasingly active northern stream storm track, up toward James\nand southern Hudson Bay, will tamp down the ridge late in the\nweekend, and drape a cold front into northern parts of the area.\nA legitimate chance for showers exists for the Straits area and\neastern upper MI late Sat night into Sunday morning. Additional\npieces of northern energy will further suppress the ridge after\nthat. Some small chances for showers early next week, but the\nbigger story is a substantial cooldown. Some highs will not\nescape the 40s, especially in the eastern UP. (Note that this is\nonly a few degrees cooler than climo.)",
